      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    fund_value = 100_000_000\n    current_share_weight = 0.80\n    target_share_weight = 0.60\n    share_beta = 1.20\n    futures_index_level = 1_200\n    futures_multiplier = 250\n    futures_beta = 0.95\n\n    # Calculate the equity exposure to be shifted\n    equity_exposure_shift = (\n        (current_share_weight - target_share_weight)\n        * fund_value\n        * share_beta\n    )\n\n    # Calculate the beta-adjusted value of one stock index futures contract\n    futures_contract_value = futures_index_level * futures_multiplier\n    beta_adjusted_contract_value = futures_contract_value * futures_beta\n\n    # Calculate the number of stock index futures contracts\n    contracts = equity_exposure_shift / beta_adjusted_contract_value\n\n    # Return the answer rounded to three decimal places\n    return round(contracts, 3)\n```",
